    thinking: "**Examining Build Configurations**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of setting up the build configurations. I\'m focusing on the `package.json` scripts, specifically the \"dev\" and \"build\" commands for an Express + Vite full-stack setup. I want to ensure these scripts properly handle both the frontend with Vite and the backend with Express using `tsx`. The build script needs careful examination.\n\n\n**Defining Server Behavior**\n\nI\'m now outlining the `server.ts` file, where I\'m integrating Express with `@google/genai` to use `gemini-3.7-flash`. The key focus is on strict grounding within the internal company documents. I\'m building in measures for preventing external browsing or assumptions, and I am configuring it to respond precisely if data isn\'t in the internal docs. I will also incorporate schema and citations in the structured output.\n\n\n**Incorporating Policy Documents**\n\nI am now integrating the actual company policy documents into the system. I\'m focusing on various formats (including `.txt`, `.md`, `.csv`, JSON, and policies) to ensure comprehensive data ingestion. I\'m focusing on the \"Strict Verification Mode\" toggle to provide exact-match citation verification. I\'m working with documents like the Employee Handbook, Security Policy, Engineering Workflow, Travel Policy, Escalation Matrix, and Product Release protocol.\n\n\n"
