    thinking: "**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve started defining the core data structures needed for this project in `src/types.ts`. I\'ve outlined `DocumentItem`, `Citation`, and `ChatMessage`, considering essential fields like IDs, titles, content, relevance scores, and roles. I\'m focusing on providing the right abstractions to allow for future flexibility and scalability as the system evolves.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been expanding the data structures with more specific types like `ChatSession`, `StrictnessMode`, and `DocGapReport` in `src/types.ts`. I am adding fields like `selectedDocIds` to `ChatSession` for doc management, defining the strictness levels, and documenting the gap reports. I\'ve also incorporated detailed sample data for real-world scenarios within `src/data/defaultDocs.ts`, adding rich test cases.\n\n\n**Analyzing Policy Guidelines**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down complex policies into digestible pieces. I\'ve extracted key details from `ENG-03`, focusing on code review SLAs, test coverage, and deployment windows. I am also extracting rules from `FIN-04`, specifically meal per diem, air travel class restrictions, and hotel rate caps to enable automated policy checking.\n\n\n**Deconstructing Policy Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of several operational policies. Specifically, I\'m parsing the \'Remote Work Policy (HR-01)\' for location requirements and \'Expense Report Policy (FIN-01)\' to extract key constraints. I\'m also analyzing \'Customer Escalation & Incident Management Runbook (OPS-05)\' for severity levels and SLAs, and dissecting \'QA Sign-Off, Feature Flagging & Rollback Procedures (QA-06)\' to understand release processes. I will start outlining all this in the server, with the Express backend.\n\n\n**Implementing API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m making progress on the API, focusing on `/api/query` and `/api/health`. The query route is now handling user questions and document selection, using `@google/genai` with `gemini-3.7-flash`. The system instruction is strict: I\'m ensuring it *only* uses provided company documents, with zero external knowledge. Direct quotes or citations are mandatory, and there\'s a negative fallback for unanswered questions. I\'m being very careful not to extrapolate.\n\n\n**Designing Response Schema**\n\nI\'m solidifying the API response schema now. I\'m focusing on a JSON structure containing the answer, a grounding indicator, confidence score, citations (with document ID, title, heading, exact quote, and relevance), and a list of the documents searched. I am also planning a `gapAnalysis` field to explain any missing information when the answer isn\'t found. Importantly, I\'m integrating robust error handling for missing or invalid API keys.\n\n**Developing Client UI**\n\nI\'m now outlining client-side UI features. I\'m designing a branded header for the internal knowledge base AI, with live verification status indicators for the grounding mode, external retrieval, and hallucination guardrails. I will also build a document knowledge base drawer/manager with options to view all internal docs, search by keywords, view formatted content, add documents via file upload (txt, md, json, csv) or paste, and the ability to edit or delete the custom documents.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 447630617
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
