    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    replacement_chunks {
      replacement_content: "import { DocumentItem } from \'../types\';\n\nexport const DEFAULT_COMPANY_DOCUMENTS: DocumentItem[] = [\n  {\n    id: \'DOC-HR-001\',\n    title: \'Employee Benefits, Leave & Remote Work Policy (2026)\',\n    category: \'HR & Benefits\',\n    lastUpdated: \'2026-01-15\',\n    version: \'4.2\',\n    author: \'People Operations Team\',\n    summary: \'Details PTO accrual rates, 401(k) employer matching, parental leave, health insurance plans, and home office stipends.\',\n    tags: [\'PTO\', \'401k\', \'benefits\', \'parental leave\', \'remote stipend\', \'healthcare\'],\n    isDefault: true,\n    content: `# Employee Benefits, Leave & Remote Work Policy (2026)\n**Document ID:** DOC-HR-001 | **Effective Date:** January 1, 2026 | **Custodian:** People Operations\n\n## 1. Paid Time Off (PTO) & Holidays\n- **Accrual Rate:** Full-time regular employees accrue 20 days (160 hours) of Paid Time Off per calendar year, accrued semi-monthly on each payroll cycle (6.67 hours per pay period).\n- **Rollover Limits:** A maximum of 5 unused PTO days may roll over into the subsequent calendar year. Any additional unused PTO beyond 5 days is forfeited on December 31 at 11:59 PM EST.\n- **Floating Holidays & Company Holidays:** The company observes 11 standard federal holidays plus 2 additional floating personal holidays per calendar year.\n- **Bereavement Leave:** Up to 5 consecutive paid business days for immediate family members (spouse, child, parent, sibling), and 3 days for extended family.\n\n## 2. Retirement & 401(k) Employer Match\n- **Eligibility:** All employees are eligible for the company 401(k) plan through Vanguard starting on their first full calendar month of employment.\n- **Match Calculation:** The company matches 100% of employee contributions up to the first 4% of eligible base salary, and 50% on the next 2% of salary. The maximum total employer matching contribution is 5.0% of base salary.\n- **Vesting Schedule:** All employer matching contributions are 100% immediately vested from day one (immediate vesting).\n\n## 3. Health, Dental & Vision Insurance\n- **Medical Provider:** UnitedHealthcare Choice Plus (HDHP with HSA contribution of $1,000/individual or $2,000/family paid by company annually) or PPO 500 Plan.\n- **Dental & Vision:** Delta Dental Premier ($2,000 annual max) and VSP Vision Care (annual eye exam 100% covered, $200 frame allowance).\n- **Wellness & Fitness Reimbursement:** $75 gross monthly allowance via Expensify under category \"Wellness\" for gym memberships, fitness classes, or mental health subscriptions.\n\n## 4. Parental & Caregiver Leave\n- **Paid Parental Leave:** All new parents (birth, adoption, foster placement, gestational carrier), regardless of gender or primary/secondary designation, are entitled to 16 continuous weeks of 100% base-salary paid leave.\n- **Eligibility:** Must have completed at least 90 calendar days of active full-time service prior to the qualifying event.\n- **Gradual Return-to-Work:** Employees may opt for an 80% schedule (4 days/week) at 100% full pay for the first 4 weeks following return from parental leave.\n\n## 5. Remote Work & Equipment Stipend\n- **Home Office Setup Stipend:** New hires receive a one-time, non-taxable $1,000 technology and ergonomic furniture allowance reimbursable within the first 60 days of employment.\n- **Monthly Internet & Utility Subsidy:** $60 net per month automatically added to the secondary monthly payroll paycheck for all designated remote/hybrid employees.\n- **Core Collaboration Hours:** Remote teams are expected to be available for real-time synchronous collaboration during core team hours: 10:00 AM to 3:00 PM in their local home time zone (EST/CST/PST).`\n  },\n  {\n    id: \'DOC-SEC-002\',\n    title: \'SOC 2 Information Security, Access Control & BYOD Policy\',\n    category: \'Security & Compliance\',\n    lastUpdated: \'2026-02-01\',\n    version: \'3.8\',\n    author: \'Chief Information Security Officer (CISO) & Infosec Team\',\n    summary: \'Standards for enterprise authentication, hardware 2FA keys, data classification, incident escalation, and remote wipe protocols.\',\n    tags: [\'SOC2\', \'security\', \'passwords\', \'2FA\', \'incident reporting\', \'encryption\', \'BYOD\'],\n    isDefault: true,\n    content: `# SOC 2 Information Security, Access Control & BYOD Policy\n**Document ID:** DOC-SEC-002 | **Classification:** Tier 2 - Internal Confidential | **Owner:** Information Security\n\n## 1. Authentication & Password Standards\n- **Password Complexity:** Passwords must be a minimum of 16 characters in length generated by the company-provided 1Password Enterprise vault. Passwords expire every 180 days if not managed via SSO.\n- **Hardware Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA):** All access to production AWS/GCP cloud environments, GitHub repositories, and customer databases strictly requires FIDO2/WebAuthn hardware security keys (YubiKey 5 Series). SMS or email OTP verification is strictly prohibited for engineering and infrastructure tier access.\n- **Screen Lock Timeout:** All workstations must be configured with an automatic screen lock triggered after 5 minutes of inactivity.\n\n## 2. Data Classification Levels\n- **Tier 1 - Public:** Marketing materials, public documentation, open-source repositories.\n- **Tier 2 - Internal Confidential:** Internal communication, strategy roadmaps, financial projections, architectural diagrams.\n- **Tier 3 - Restricted (PII/Financial):** Customer personal identifiable information (PII), payment credentials, hashed passwords, production encryption secrets. Tier 3 data must be encrypted at rest with AES-256 and in transit via TLS 1.3.\n\n## 3. Security Incident Reporting & Escalation Protocol\n- **Reporting Window:** Any suspected security anomaly, lost device, credential leak, or unauthorized access attempt MUST be reported within 30 minutes of discovery.\n- **Designated Channels:** Submit directly to \\`security@company.internal\\` or page the on-call security engineer in the private Slack channel \\`#sec-incident-hotline\\`.\n- **Public Disclosure Prohibition:** Employees are strictly prohibited from discussing or sharing potential security vulnerabilities or breaches on external social media, personal channels, or customer-facing forums without written authorization from Legal and the CISO.\n\n## 4. Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) & Mobile Device Management (MDM)\n- **Workstation Mandate:** Company-issued MacBooks or ThinkPads managed through Kandji/Jamf MDM must be used for all primary engineering, sales, and executive work.\n- **Disk Encryption:** Full-disk encryption (FileVault for macOS, BitLocker for Windows) must remain enabled at 100% capacity at all times.\n- **Personal Mobile Devices:** Accessing work email (Google Workspace) or Slack from personal mobile devices requires enrollment in the company MDM with remote-wipe permissions for company containers.`\n  },\n  {\n    id: \'DOC-ENG-003\',\n    title: \'Engineering Standards, Code Reviews & Deployment Windows\',\n    category: \'Engineering\',\n    lastUpdated: \'2026-02-10\',\n    version: \'5.1\',\n    author: \'Engineering Architecture Council\',\n    summary: \'Pull request approval requirements, code coverage minimums, production deployment freeze schedules, and on-call SLAs.\',\n    tags: [\'engineering\', \'code review\', \'PR approvals\', \'deployment freeze\', \'CI/CD\', \'on-call\'],\n    isDefault: true,\n    content: `# Engineering Standards, Code Reviews & Deployment Windows\n**Document ID:** DOC-ENG-003 | **Effective Date:** February 2026 | **Custodian:** Engineering Council\n\n## 1. Pull Request & Code Review SLAs\n- **Review Turnaround Time:** Pull requests must receive an initial code review within 24 business hours of submission. Urgent bug fixes tagged \\`[P0-Fix]\\` must be reviewed within 2 hours.\n- **Required Approvals:**\n  - Standard Microservices: Minimum 1 peer code review approval from a code owner in the \\`CODEOWNERS\\` file.\n  - Core Auth, Billing, and Data Pipeline Services: Minimum 2 approvals, including at least one Senior or Staff Staff Engineer.\n- **Automated Checks:** All CI/CD pipelines must pass 100% of linting, type-checking, and automated regression suites prior to merge.\n\n## 2. Test Coverage & Quality Gates\n- **Unit Test Coverage:** New code merged into main branches must maintain or increase total test coverage, with a hard minimum of 85% branch coverage for business logic in domain packages.\n- **Integration Testing:** Any change altering an external REST or gRPC contract must include an updated end-to-end contract test suite.\n\n## 3. Production Deployment Windows & Freeze Periods\n- **Authorized Deployment Windows:** Production releases are permitted exclusively Tuesday through Thursday between 10:00 AM EST and 3:00 PM EST.\n- **Deployment Freezes:**\n  - **Friday / Weekend Freeze:** Deployments are prohibited from Friday 12:00 PM EST through Monday 9:00 AM EST to preserve service stability.\n  - **Holiday Freeze:** End-of-year deployment freeze runs from December 15 through January 5 annually.\n  - **Emergency Override:** Emergency hotfixes during freeze windows require explicit two-party approval from the VP of Engineering and the incident commander.\n\n## 4. Zero-Downtime Database Migrations\n- **Expand/Contract Pattern:** Database schema migrations must never introduce breaking column drops or renames in a single step. All schema changes must follow the 3-phase Expand, Migrate, Contract lifecycle with backwards compatibility for the previous two application versions.\n\n## 5. On-Call Responsibilities & Pager Duty SLA\n- **Primary On-Call Response Time:** Must acknowledge and begin triage on P0/P1 alerts within 15 minutes 24/7. Secondary backup is automatically paged if unacknowledged after 20 minutes.\n- **On-Call Compensation:** Engineers receive $450 per week of primary on-call rotation plus 1.5x hourly equivalent for active remediation time beyond scheduled working hours.`\n  },\n  {\n    id: \'DOC-FIN-004\',\n    title: \'Corporate Travel, Meals & Expense Reimbursement Guidelines\',\n    category: \'Finance & Travel\',\n    lastUpdated: \'2026-01-20\',\n    version: \'3.4\',\n    author: \'Finance & Accounting Operations\',\n    summary: \'Rules for booking domestic and international flights, per diem meal limits, hotel tier maximums, and Expensify submission deadlines.\',\n    tags: [\'travel\', \'meals\', \'per diem\', \'hotels\', \'flights\', \'expenses\', \'reimbursement\'],\n    isDefault: true,\n    content: `# Corporate Travel, Meals & Expense Reimbursement Guidelines\n**Document ID:** DOC-FIN-004 | **Audience:** All Global Employees | **Owner:** Finance Department\n\n## 1. Flight Booking & Travel Classes\n- **Domestic Flights (under 6 hours):** Must be booked in standard Economy / Main Cabin via the corporate travel portal (Navan). Economy Plus / Extra Legroom is approved for employees taller than 6\'2\" or with documented medical needs.\n- **International Flights & Long-Haul:** Business Class (or Premium Economy if Business is unavailable) is permitted only for non-stop flights exceeding 6 continuous flight hours, subject to Director-level pre-approval.\n- **Advance Booking:** Flights must be booked at least 14 days in advance of departure unless responding to an urgent customer escalation.\n\n## 2. Daily Meal Allowances (Per Diem)\n- **Domestic US Travel:** Maximum daily meal reimbursement is $85 USD per full travel day (allocated as $20 Breakfast, $25 Lunch, $40 Dinner). No itemized split is required as long as the total daily aggregate does not exceed $85.\n- **International Travel & High-Cost Metro (SF, NYC, London, Zurich, Tokyo):** Maximum daily meal allowance is $120 USD per full travel day.\n- **Alcohol Policy:** Alcoholic beverages are reimbursable up to a maximum of $25 per day as part of dinner meals, provided meals are consumed during legitimate business travel.\n\n## 3. Lodging & Hotel Nightly Caps\n- **Standard Tier Cities:** Maximum reimbursable room rate is $250 USD per night (excluding mandatory city taxes and resort fees).\n- **High-Cost Tier 1 Cities (New York, San Francisco, Boston, London, Paris, Tokyo):** Maximum room rate is $350 USD per night.\n- **Airbnb / Short-Term Rentals:** Approved only for stays exceeding 4 consecutive nights and when the total cost is at least 15% lower than the equivalent corporate hotel rate.\n\n## 4. Expense Submission Deadlines & Receipts\n- **Submission Window:** All expense reports must be submitted via Expensify within 30 calendar days of the transaction date or travel completion date.\n- **Receipt Threshold:** Itemized receipts are mandatory for any single transaction exceeding $25 USD. Credit card statements without itemized receipts are not accepted for meal or lodging expenses.`\n  },\n  {\n    id: \'DOC-OPS-005\',\n    title: \'Customer Escalations, Severity Levels & Incident Response Matrix\',\n    category: \'Operations\',\n    lastUpdated: \'2026-02-05\',\n    version: \'4.0\',\n    author: \'Customer Success & Site Reliability Engineering (SRE)\',\n    summary: \'Defines incident severity tiers (P0-P3), customer communication cadence, executive war room triggers, and Root Cause Analysis (RCA) deadlines.\',\n    tags: [\'incident response\', \'SLA\', \'escalations\', \'severity levels\', \'RCA\', \'customer support\'],\n    isDefault: true,\n    content: `# Customer Escalations, Severity Levels & Incident Response Matrix\n**Document ID:** DOC-OPS-005 | **Classification:** Internal Operations | **Custodian:** SRE & CS Operations\n\n## 1. Incident Severity Definitions\n- **P0 - Catastrophic Outage:** Complete platform unavailability or data loss affecting >25% of active customers or any Tier-1 enterprise account during business hours.\n- **P1 - Major Core Feature Outage:** Critical system functionality unavailable (e.g., checkout API failing, authentication down for a subset of regions) with no immediate workaround.\n- **P2 - Degraded Performance / Workaround Available:** Subsystem slowness, non-critical feature outage, or UI latency with an operational workaround.\n- **P3 - Minor Issue / Cosmetic Defect:** Low impact bug, typo, styling flaw, or single-user intermittent edge case.\n\n## 2. Incident Response & Communication SLAs\n| Severity | Initial Response SLA | Status Page Update Cadence | Internal Exec Briefing |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **P0** | **< 15 minutes** | Every 30 minutes | Within 30 mins |\n| **P1** | **< 30 minutes** | Every 60 minutes | Within 2 hours |\n| **P2** | **< 2 hours** | On resolution / daily | Daily summary |\n| **P3** | **< 24 hours** | Release notes | Weekly sprint review |\n\n## 3. Incident Commander & War Room Procedures\n- **Automated War Room:** For any P0 or P1 incident, the on-call SRE immediately invokes the Slack workflow \\`/incident create\\`, which spins up a dedicated incident channel \\`#inc-YYYYMMDD-service\\` and a Google Meet war room link.\n- **Roles:** The Incident Commander (IC) leads triage; the Communications Lead manages customer status page postings; the Tech Lead directs debugging.\n- **Root Cause Analysis (RCA) Policy:** An un-blamable Post-Incident Review (PIR) and RCA document must be published and reviewed within 5 business days for all P0 and P1 events.`\n  },\n  {\n    id: \'DOC-PROD-006\',\n    title: \'Product Release Lifecycle, Feature Flagging & QA Sign-Off\',\n    category: \'Product\',\n    lastUpdated: \'2026-01-28\',\n    version: \'2.9\',\n    author: \'Product Operations & QA Engineering\',\n    summary: \'Standard release stages, canary rollout percentage gates, LaunchDarkly feature flag hygiene, and instant rollback procedures.\',\n    tags: [\'product release\', \'QA\', \'feature flags\', \'canary rollout\', \'rollback\', \'LaunchDarkly\'],\n    isDefault: true,\n    content: `# Product Release Lifecycle, Feature Flagging & QA Sign-Off\n**Document ID:** DOC-PROD-006 | **Scope:** Product Management & Quality Engineering\n\n## 1. Release Milestone Stages\n- **Stage 0 - Local & Preview Sandbox:** Feature complete and validated against automated test suites.\n- **Stage 1 - Staging & Internal Dogfooding (Alpha):** Deployed to the internal dogfood cluster for employee testing for a minimum of 72 hours.\n- **Stage 2 - Canary Beta (10% Traffic):** Enabled for 10% of standard non-enterprise accounts. Monitored for error budget spikes (error rate must remain below 0.05%).\n- **Stage 3 - General Availability (GA - 100%):** Full rollout following 48 hours of stable telemetry in Stage 2.\n\n## 2. Feature Flagging Standards\n- **Flag Tooling:** All new customer-facing features must be wrapped in a LaunchDarkly boolean or multivariate feature flag.\n- **Flag Retirement:** Feature flags must be scheduled for complete code removal within 30 days of reaching 100% GA status to avoid technical debt.\n- **Kill-Switch Requirement:** Every high-risk feature flag must include a server-side circuit breaker configured to disable automatically if error rates exceed 1.0% over 5 minutes.\n\n## 3. Instant Rollback Playbook\n- **Rollback Trigger:** If a release causes >0.5% error rates or latency degradation >200ms for more than 5 minutes, the release manager initiates an immediate rollback.\n- **Execution Command:** Automated rollback via GitHub Actions workflow \\`deploy-rollback.yml\\` or terminal command \\`company-cli deploy rollback --env=prod --target=previous\\`. Total rollback time must complete within 90 seconds.`\n  }\n];\n\nexport const SAMPLE_QUERIES = [\n  {\n    label: \'401(k) Matching\',\n    query: \'What is our company 401(k) match and when does it vest?\',\n    category: \'HR & Benefits\',\n    expectedDoc: \'DOC-HR-001\',\n    shouldBeFound: true\n  },\n  {\n    label: \'Production Deployment Hours\',\n    query: \'When are we allowed to deploy code to production, and are Friday deployments permitted?\',\n    category: \'Engineering\',\n    expectedDoc: \'DOC-ENG-003\',\n    shouldBeFound: true\n  },\n  {\n    label: \'Meal Per Diem & Travel\',\n    query: \'What is the daily meal per diem for domestic vs international travel, and can I expense alcohol?\',\n    category: \'Finance & Travel\',\n    expectedDoc: \'DOC-FIN-004\',\n    shouldBeFound: true\n  },\n  {\n    label: \'Security Incident Escalation\',\n    query: \'How quickly must a security incident be reported, and through which channels?\',\n    category: \'Security & Compliance\',\n    expectedDoc: \'DOC-SEC-002\',\n    shouldBeFound: true\n  },\n  {\n    label: \'Parental Leave Duration\',\n    query: \'How many weeks of paid parental leave do new parents receive, and who is eligible?\',\n    category: \'HR & Benefits\',\n    expectedDoc: \'DOC-HR-001\',\n    shouldBeFound: true\n  },\n  {\n    label: \'P0 Incident Response SLA\',\n    query: \'What is the response SLA and update frequency for a P0 critical outage?\',\n    category: \'Operations\',\n    expectedDoc: \'DOC-OPS-005\',\n    shouldBeFound: true\n  },\n  {\n    label: \'External Out-of-Scope Test #1\',\n    query: \'Who won the 2024 Super Bowl?\',\n    category: \'Strict Negative Test\',\n    expectedDoc: \'None\',\n    shouldBeFound: false\n  },\n  {\n    label: \'External Out-of-Scope Test #2\',\n    query: \'What is the stock price of Apple today and what is their latest iPhone model?\',\n    category: \'Strict Negative Test\',\n    expectedDoc: \'None\',\n    shouldBeFound: false\n  },\n  {\n    label: \'External Out-of-Scope Test #3\',\n    query: \'How do I change the oil in a 2018 Toyota Camry?\',\n    category: \'Strict Negative Test\',\n    expectedDoc: \'None\',\n    shouldBeFound: false\n  }\n];\n"
    }
