    thinking: "**Defining Component Hierarchy**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on the React component structure. I\'ve begun outlining the necessary components, starting with `Header.tsx`. This includes branding elements like the Shield/Lock/Book icons and also critical \"Live Security & Grounding Status\" indicators. I\'m prioritizing a visually appealing and user-friendly experience.\n\n\n**Expanding Component Definitions**\n\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out specific modal components. The `DocumentModal` will handle full document display with navigation and editing. Next, the `AddDocumentModal` will enable user document uploads, supporting various formats and metadata input. Then I will implement a `CitationInspector` for inspecting quotations and sources and finally the `DocumentGapModal`, which will aid in knowledge gap identification.\n\n\n**Developing Sidebar Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the knowledge base sidebar. It will feature a quick search, with filters to select document sets and display stats like word count and last updated. I\'m focusing on user-friendly document selection via checkbox and clear, concise document overviews. I have started on the drawer implementation now.\n\n\n"
