sizing the matched internal documentation\n+  const docName = bestMatch.doc.title.split(\',\')[0];\n+  const mainContentClean = bestMatch.text\n+    .replace(/^#+\\s*/gm, \'### \')\n+    .trim();\n+\n+  let formattedAnswer = `According to **${docName}**`;\n+  if (bestMatch.heading && bestMatch.heading !== docName) {\n+    formattedAnswer += ` (*${bestMatch.heading}*)`;\n+  }\n+  formattedAnswer += `:\\n\\n${mainContentClean}\\n\\n`;\n+\n+  if (matchedSections.length > 1 && matchedSections[1].doc.id !== bestMatch.doc.id) {\n+    const sec = matchedSections[1];\n+    formattedAnswer += `\\n**Additional Reference from ${sec.doc.title.split(\',\')[0]}:**\\n${sec.text.slice(0, 250).trim()}...`;\n+  }\n+\n+  const finalConfidence = Math.min(0.99, 0.70 + (bestMatch.score * 0.05));\n+\n+  return {\n+    isGrounded: true,\n+    answer: formattedAnswer,\n+    citations,\n+    confidenceScore: finalConfidence,\n+    searchedDocs: docTitles,\n+    status: \'grounded\'\n+  };\n+}\n+\n+\n[diff_block_end]\n\nPlease note that the above snippet only shows the MODIFIED lines from the last change. It shows up to 3 lines of unchanged lines before and after the modified lines. The actual file contents may have many more lines not shown.The following action was requested:\nRunning linter...The action produced the following result:\nLinting completed successfully\nOutput:\n\n> react-example@0.0.0 lint\n> tsc --noEmit\n\nThe following action was requested:\nBuilding applet...The action produced the following result:\nBuild succeeded - the applet is compiledThe following action was requested:\nRestarting dev server...The action produced the following result:\nDev server restarted successfully"
